# Target C: branch-adaptive physical pentagon closure secants

Date: 2026-09-19

Status: exact local nonlinear-to-polyhedral consequence; theorem-state authority unchanged. C-II remains open.

The current generic H6 endpoint has 4,976 cells after the one-face order-hull reduction. The immediate linear attack is to retain the full local split into ten physical gap orders times the median-low/high bit. This note strengthens that 20-branch layer before rerunning the global census.

## Setup

For normalized cyclic force gaps `x_i=delta_i/pi`, the established sharp two-gap closure theorem is

\[
x_{k+2}+x_{k+3}\le M(x_k),
\]

where

\[
M(x)=2\left[1-\frac1\pi\arccos\left(\frac12-\cos\frac{\pi x}{2}\right)\right].
\]

The function `M` is convex on the physical interval. Therefore if `M(a)<=U_a` and `M(b)<=U_b`, the chord through `(a,U_a)` and `(b,U_b)` is a valid rational upper bound for `M` throughout `[a,b]`.

Fix the representative physical gap order

\[
x_a\le x_b\le x_c\le x_d\le x_e.
\]

The previously certified rank-threshold theorem gives the following outer intervals.

On the median-low branch `x_c<=2/5`:

\[
\begin{aligned}
0&\le x_a\le2/5,\\
4/15&\le x_b\le2/5,\\
1/3&\le x_c\le2/5,\\
2/5&\le x_d\le2/3,\\
2/5&\le x_e\le2/3.
\end{aligned}
\]

On the median-high branch `x_c>=2/5`:

\[
\begin{aligned}
1/15&\le x_a\le2/5,\\
1/6&\le x_b\le2/5,\\
2/5&\le x_c\le1/2,\\
2/5&\le x_d\le3/5,\\
2/5&\le x_e\le2/3.
\end{aligned}
\]

The old order-hull reduction used only the broad exact secants

\[
M(x)\le\frac23+\frac{x}{3}\quad(0\le x\le2/5)
\]

and

\[
M(x)\le\frac12+\frac{3x}{4}\quad(2/5\le x\le2/3).
\]

Those throw away most of the branchwise interval information.

## New exact endpoint certificates

`verify_target_c_pentagon_branch_adaptive_secants_2026_09_19.py` repeats the rational Machin enclosure for `pi` and the alternating Taylor lower bound for cosine used by the existing all-rank secant verifier. It certifies three additional knots:

\[
\boxed{M(1/15)\le670687/10^6,}
\]

\[
\boxed{M(4/15)\le728581/10^6,}
\]

\[
\boxed{M(3/5)\le944043/10^6.}
\]

It also rechecks the existing rational endpoint certificates at `1/6`, `1/3`, and `1/2`, and the exact values

\[
M(0)=2/3,\qquad M(2/5)=4/5,\qquad M(2/3)=1.
\]

No floating-point value is used for acceptance.

## Median-low branch

For ranks `a,b,c,d,e`, respectively, convexity gives the valid upper lines

\[
\boxed{M(x_a)\le\frac23+\frac{x_a}{3},}
\]

\[
\boxed{M(x_b)\le\frac{214257}{400000}x_b+\frac{585743}{1000000},}
\]

\[
\boxed{M(x_c)\le\frac{115689}{200000}x_c+\frac{284311}{500000},}
\]

\[
\boxed{M(x_d)\le\frac12+\frac{3x_d}{4},}
\]

\[
\boxed{M(x_e)\le\frac12+\frac{3x_e}{4}.}
\]

The second-smallest and median cuts are strictly stronger than the broad low secant in the interior of their branch intervals.

## Median-high branch

The five valid upper lines are

\[
\boxed{M(x_a)\le\frac{387939}{1000000}x_a+\frac{1612061}{2500000},}
\]

\[
\boxed{M(x_b)\le\frac{325671}{700000}x_b+\frac{1074329}{1750000},}
\]

\[
\boxed{M(x_c)\le\frac{67191}{100000}x_c+\frac{132809}{250000},}
\]

\[
\boxed{M(x_d)\le\frac{144043}{200000}x_d+\frac{255957}{500000},}
\]

\[
\boxed{M(x_e)\le\frac12+\frac{3x_e}{4}.}
\]

Thus four of the five rank positions become strictly tighter than the broad low/high secants on the interior of their branch intervals. Only the maximum retains the old high secant.

## Consequence for the finite H6 attack

The correct next one-face system is stronger than the previously proposed plain median split. For each of the ten gap orders, keep two closed median branches and attach the five branch-adaptive chords above. This gives twenty local polyhedral branches per physical face.

A generic H6 cell is eliminated if all twenty branches at one physical face have exact rational Farkas contradictions against the 85-variable complete-angle system. Because the branches cover the rank-threshold closures including the regular equality case, no physical pentagon is lost by the split.

This theorem does not itself change the 4,976-cell census. Its purpose is to strengthen the exact branch system before the next exhaustive reduction. If one-face branching saturates, the same twenty-way local description is the appropriate node system for multi-face branch-and-bound. The fifteen complete reciprocal sine-law consistency equations remain the nonlinear layer after the affine disjunction is exhausted.
